Subject: Preservation scope for SP26-097765


CAUTION:  This email originated from outside of OSP.  Do not click links or=
 open attachments unless you know the content is safe.
I received your letter of July 23, 2026 regarding the litigation hold for C=
AD event SP26-097765. Thank you for confirming the hold and for identifying=
 the standard by which it operates.

My case is not resolved. This message serves as the confirmation your lette=
r requests, and I will continue to confirm at the intervals you describe.

Because your letter states the hold applies to any record included in my pr=
eservation request, I am setting out that scope explicitly so there is no a=
mbiguity about what is covered. The following are all associated with the M=
arch 24, 2026 contact at my residence on restricted federal land in the Sil=
tcoos corridor of the Siuslaw National Forest, Lane County, Oregon, reached=
 through a locked gate off Siltcoos Beach Access Road.

1. CAD event SP26-097765 in full, including the complete audit trail, all e=
dits, all entries and deletions, all timestamps, all user identifiers, and =
any field showing when and by whom my date of birth was entered.

2. All recorded dispatch communications relating to that event, including r=
adio traffic, telephone lines, and any recorded call preceding or following=
 it.

3. All body-worn camera and in-car video recordings from every officer pres=
ent or dispatched, in original unedited form, including any footage recorde=
d before arrival and after departure from the location.

4. All incident reports, supplemental reports, officer notes, and after-act=
ion documentation.

5. All electronic communications concerning me, this event, my name, my dat=
e of birth, my residence, the domain oprdvolunteerabuse.org, or my online a=
ctivity, including email, text messages, and messaging on any state or pers=
onal device used for state business.

6. All communications between any Oregon State Police employee and any empl=
oyee of the Oregon Parks and Recreation Department, the United States Fores=
t Service, or the Oregon Department of Justice concerning me or this event.

7. Any record reflecting the source of my date of birth and the manner in w=
hich it entered any Oregon State Police system.

8. Any record reflecting the basis for the event's classification, includin=
g unit type, priority, call type, and the comment field entry stating the v=
isit was made for the Forest Service.

9. All records concerning my public records requests PR27478 and PR36445, i=
ncluding internal communications regarding the search conducted, the respon=
ses issued, the fee assessed, and the exemption applied.

10. All backup copies, archived copies, and system snapshots of any of the =
above.

I ask that the hold suspend any automated deletion, overwriting, or retenti=
on-schedule disposition applicable to these categories, including any short=
 retention period governing body-worn camera footage.

Please confirm that the hold as applied covers this scope, and identify any=
 category listed above that it does not cover.

Regards,

Robert Samuel White

